# =============================================================================
# Aura .gitignore
#
# Tailored to this repo. Verified with `git check-ignore` against the actual
# working tree - see the notes on native binaries near the bottom, which use
# negation rules that are easy to get subtly wrong.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets  (MOST IMPORTANT RULE IN THIS FILE)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .env holds the PsySeg license/access keys and the SerpAPI key. It must never
# be committed. .env.example is the redacted template and IS tracked.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# .mcp.json configures MCP servers for this repo and carries a live CV-Hub
# bearer token in an Authorization header. Same rule as .env: never commit it.
.mcp.json

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dependencies and build output
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
jspm_packages/

# electron-builder output (installers are ~125 MB each)
dist/

# Built installers copied out of dist/ for distribution. Same reason dist/ is
# ignored -- 125 MB each, and git history cannot practically shed them later.
# The prerequisites wizard and its assets under installer/ ARE tracked; only
# the built binaries are not.
installer/*.exe

# NuGet packages restored into the native projects
packages/

# NOTE: the top-level build/ directory is NOT ignored - it holds icon.ico and
# installer.nsh, which are source assets the installer needs.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Aura runtime and user data
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The SQLite DB, the user's image library, recorded audio, imports and the
# session/PID file. All generated at runtime and personal to each machine.
# The app recreates what it needs (see sessionTracker.js mkdirSync).
/data/

# Per-service logs written by attachServiceLogging() in dev mode.
/logs/
logs/
*.log

# Output of Diagnose Aura.bat, if anyone runs it inside the repo.
aura-diagnostics.txt

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python (speech service)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The venv is ~292 MB. It currently self-excludes via a .gitignore that the
# venv module writes inside itself - do not rely on that, it disappears if the
# environment is ever recreated by different tooling.
/services/speech/venv/
venv/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Visual Studio / MSBuild  (native/)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .vs/ alone was ~1.7 GB of precompiled-header cache in this tree.
.vs/
ipch/
*.VC.db
*.VC.VC.opendb
*.user
*.suo
*.sdf
*.opensdf
*.aps

# Intermediate build artifacts
*.obj
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.exp
*.idb
*.iobj
*.ipdb
*.tlog
*.pch
*.res
*.lastbuildstate
*.recipe

# Build output directories
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/
x64/
x86/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Native binaries the installer SHIPS  (deliberately tracked)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOTHING is tracked out of the Visual Studio output folders above. The
# binaries we ship are copied into native/runtime/ by scripts/stage-resources.js
# (run automatically by `npm run dist`), and tracked from there.
#
# That was not just tidiness: the vendored VCamSample project ships its own
# native/external/VCamSample/.gitignore whose `x64/` rule excludes the parent
# directory, and git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is
# excluded - so those binaries were untrackable in place at any price.

# Curated staging area for the binaries we ship - NOT a build output
# directory, so it is tracked normally.
!native/runtime/

# ...except the staged Node runtime, which is ~100 MB and is re-staged on
# every build from the interpreter running the build (process.execPath). No
# reason to carry it. Named node.exe on Windows, node on Linux.
native/runtime/node.exe
native/runtime/node

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor / tooling
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Claude Code configuration is local-only and NOT tracked. The hooks under
# .claude/hooks/ register this machine's CV-Hub integration: they POST session
# metadata to the endpoint in CV_HUB_API using the token in CV_HUB_PAT. They
# carry no secrets themselves and no-op without those credentials, but they are
# developer tooling rather than part of Aura, and anything under .claude/ runs
# automatically for whoever opens the repo. Keeping them out of the repository
# means cloning Aura never executes someone else's telemetry hooks.
.claude/

# CV-Git per-machine state. Written by `cv init`, and it records an absolute
# repository root ("C:\\Projects\\aura") plus a locally-generated repoId used
# to name this machine's graph/vector databases. Committing it would hand
# every teammate a path that does not exist on their machine. Each developer
# runs `cv init` themselves.
.cv/
.vscode/
!.vscode/extensions.json
*.code-workspace

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS noise
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
.DS_Store

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Misc Node
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.npm
.eslintcache
*.tgz
.node_repl_history
report.[0-9]*.[0-9]*.[0-9]*.[0-9]*.json
*.pid
*.seed
*.pid.lock
coverage/
*.lcov
.nyc_output
